    fix(yang.python.antlr): the linked emission requires yang.call in py's module tree; ordinary and SCC modules require and pin it before py
    
    The root cause of the linked-import reds: py's manifest pinned
    yang.call but py's module AST never issued the require, so the runtime
    was invisible inside py's closure; ordinary module emission skipped
    yang.call entirely. The module tree now requires it, and ordinary and
    SCC source modules require and pin it before py when their bodies
    reference the convention. The scanner pins regenerated (:py only,
    double-run byte-identical); import-test passes unfiltered — 50 tests /
    436 assertions / 0 failures, slow bodies included; float-address
    12/105, call-entry 3/12, call 4/15, publication 10/85; the closure
    ledgers match 156/154/155 with 148 shared; kondo 0/0; cljstyle clean.

